Step 3 — Interpret Each of Your Top Three Types
For each of your top three RIASEC types, respond to the following prompts:

My Top Three Types — Detailed Interpretation
Type 1: C — Conventional

What this type typically values: [Your response — based on the description above and your assessment results]

Interests involve organization, structure, accuracy, and working with information or data. People with this interest usually like having clear goals and finding organized and efficient ways to complete tasks.

How this shows up in my life: (Think about your hobbies, favorite school subjects, activities you lose track of time doing, volunteer work, or part-time jobs.) 

It makes sense for me because I like being organized, even if it is in a messy way sometimes, and having a plan for what needs to get done.
I enjoy working with numbers and figuring out how different pieces fit together, which is probably why math has always been my favorite subject.
At Topgolf, this also shows up in how I track inventory for the areas I am responsible for and reorganize produce so the most commonly used items are easier to access.

Careers associated with this type that interest me: (List at least 3 from the ONET results or your own research.)*

Accountant
Financial Analyst
Financial Manager

Type 2: E — Enterprising
What this type typically values: 

Interests involve leadership, decision-making, business, and taking initiative. People with this interest often enjoy leading projects, influencing decisions, solving problems, and working toward specific goals.

How this shows up in my life: 

This is probably the part of my results that I expected the most. I enjoy taking leadership roles, making decisions, and working with others to solve problems.
This shows up in my job as a Kitchen Manager/Events Chef at Topgolf, where I lead a team and help keep the kitchen running, as well as my previous experience as a Shift Lead at Sonic.
I like having responsibility and being someone others can rely on.

Careers associated with this type that interest me:

Management Consultant
Financial Manager
Business Manager

Type 3: I — Investigative

What this type typically values: 

Interests involve analyzing information, solving complex problems, learning how things work, and finding answers.
People with this interest tend to enjoy using logic, research, and data to understand problems and develop solutions.

How this shows up in my life: 

I like problems where I have to figure out what is going on and find a way to fix it.
This comes up a lot at Topgolf when something in the kitchen isn't working as well as it could, and I have to figure out a better way to do it. 
I also like working with numbers and understanding why something happened instead of just knowing that it did.

Careers associated with this type that interest me:

Data Scientist
Financial Analyst
Business Analyst

